 "narration": [
  "I audit EDGE buildings. Here are ten gaps I keep finding between the design and the site.",
  "One. Low-e glass in the model, plain glass in the frame. Two. Shading fins, cut shorter than the drawings.",
  "Three. Roof insulation, thinner than specified, or missing. Four. The cool roof paint that never got painted.",
  "Five. Low-flow taps, swapped for cheaper, thirstier ones. Six. Air conditioners less efficient than the ones in the model.",
  "Seven. Occupancy sensors on the plan, but not on the ceiling. Eight. A solar array smaller than the one in the model.",
  "Nine. AAC blocks in the model, red brick on site. Ten. No datasheets, no invoices, no photos. If it isn't documented, it didn't happen.",
  "Most of this isn't bad faith. It's value engineering nobody told the model about. So update the model before the audit, not after."
 ],
